.TH JRUBY 1 "<%= display_date %>" "JRuby" "JRuby Programmer's Reference Guide"
.SH NAME
jruby \- Interpreted object-oriented scripting language
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B <%= man_escape(synopsis_cmd) %>
<%= man_escape(synopsis_rest) %>
.SH DESCRIPTION
JRuby is a pure-Java implementation of the Ruby programming language.
It is an interpreted scripting language for quick and easy
object-oriented programming, with many features for processing text files
and for system management tasks.
The command-line switches accepted by the interpreter are described below;
they are largely similar to those of
.BR ruby (1)
and
.BR perl (1).
.SH OPTIONS
The switches are also listed in abbreviated form by
.B jruby --help
.PP
